<!--
  PATHS ARE RELATIVE, DELIBERATELY (fixed 2026-09-10).

  This file used to use absolute /media/fat/... paths, described as "belt-and-
  braces -- honored verbatim on every Main version". That reasoning only holds if
  the games live on the SD card. MEASURED: with games on a USB drive, /media/fat
  paths do not exist, NONE of the file entries load, and the core falls back to
  autoloading a boot.rom -- finding the CONSUMER SONY BIOS in games/PSX, because
  the core reports its CONF_STR name to Main as "PSX". Symptom: the PlayStation
  logo and startup sound instead of the Konami BIOS.

  Relative paths resolve against whichever storage the launcher was started from,
  so this works on SD and USB alike. For an SD-only setup the equivalent absolute
  path is /media/fat/<path below>.

  Belt-and-braces that does work: put a copy of the standard BIOS at
  games/System573/boot.rom. If Main resolves this core's HomeDir from <setname>,
  that autoload finds the Konami BIOS rather than the Sony one.
-->
<!--
  BIOS POST SMOKE TEST (one file, no game data).

  Loads a 573 BIOS and nothing else. The board reaches the GX700 power-on
  self-test and stops at `CDR BAD` -- expected, since the self-test is sequential
  and there is no CD attached and no flash image staged. That is still a useful
  test: reaching it proves the R3000 executes the BIOS from SDRAM, every probed
  RAM/ROM position reads back, rtl/s573_io.v answers the 18E I/O-MCU check, the
  GPU renders text and video scans out. Verified 2026-09-10 on a DE10.

  NOTE: this file used to be described as launching Gacha Gachamp. It does not.
  `700a01(gchgchmp).22g` is a BIOS *revision* found on that hardware, not a
  game-in-BIOS -- MAME's gchgchmp needs eight flash ROMs, eight PCMCIA card ROMs
  and a security cassette. Measured: this BIOS and the standard BIOS give a
  byte-identical self-test screen. See dumps/README.md.

  To actually boot a game, use hyperbbc_console.mgl.

  Requires: _Console/Konami_System_573.rbf +
            games/System573/573bios_gchgchmp.bin
-->
<mistergamedescription>
  <rbf>_Console/Konami_System_573</rbf>
  <setname>System573</setname>
  <file delay="1" type="f" index="0" path="games/System573/573bios_gchgchmp.bin"/>
  <reset delay="1"/>
</mistergamedescription>
